        {
          "id": "abbotsleigh2025-ext2-q16a_iii",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "timeLimit": 60,
          "stem": "Using \\(kI_k=I_{k+1}-I_k+4^{-k-1}e^{-1/4}\\), what sum follows for k=1 to n?",
          "hint": "Sum the recurrence; the I-terms telescope and the remaining powers form a geometric series.",
          "solution": "The first expression.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Sum both sides.",
              "work": "\\(\\sum kI_k=\\sum(I_{k+1}-I_k)+\\frac1{e^{1/4}}\\sum(1/4)^{k+1}.\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Telescope the integral terms.",
              "work": "\\(\\sum(I_{k+1}-I_k)=I_{n+1}-I_1.\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Sum the geometric series.",
              "work": "\\(\\sum_{k=1}^n(1/4)^{k+1}=\\frac1{12}(1-(1/4)^n).\\)"
            }
          ],
          "xp": 1,
          "meta": {
